        <detaileddescription>
<para>This constructor sets everything needed by the algorithm. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">X0</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>This is the starting point of the search. It is stored as the data member, _x0. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Epsilon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The is used to define the end point of the iterative procedure, do_iteration. The loop will terminate when the abs(F(xi) - fsolve)) is less than Epsilon. It is stored as the data member, _epsilon. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Twice_df</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If Twice_df then the derivative of F, at point i, is approximated as (F(x[i])+f(x[i-1])*.5 which approximates the derivative of F over the interval x[i] to x[i-1]. It is stored as the data member, _F. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">max_iter</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The maximum number of iterations before do_iteration, will terminate. It is stored as the data member _max_iter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">F</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>This reference to a functor object serves as the object for calling the member function pointers f, df and d2f. It is stored as the data member _F. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">f</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>This pointer to a member function is used to calculate the function to solved. It is stored as the data member _f. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">df</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>This pointer to a member function is used to calculate the derivative of the function to solved. It is stored as the data member _df. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">d2f</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>This pointer to a member function is used to calculate the second derivative of the function to solved. It is stored as the data member _d2f. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">fsolve</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>This is the value of f to be solved. It&apos;s default value is 0. It is stored as the data member _fsolve. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">check_boundary</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If true then the algorithm will check constrain the search so that it only stays within min_x and max_x. If the search goes outside of the range then the solution is set to the boundary value. It is stored as the data member _check_boundary. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
